  "actual_scope": "Live related issue bodies/comments and PR1158; exact-ID and contextual GitHub issue searches in MIM and KG-Microbe; current MIM maintained source/index text searches including ignored files. No scientific review of whole contextual owners.",
  "native_owner_claim": null,
  "local_owner_conclusion": "No exact source ID or raw damaged attribute match in data, mappings, docs/data and UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING.tsv under gitignore-independent rg. This is bounded absence, not proof of complete source-model absence. Frozen owners[] and no identity-bearing source label remain consistent with no identified MIM owner.",
  "contextual_comparator": "Yeast_Extract.yaml has catalog aliases and FOODON:03315426 but no connection to exact blank source1944 demonstrated by these searches. The recipe-specific preparation fragment must not become a generic yeast alias.",
  "deduplication_conclusion": "No exact1944 issue was found in the successful bounded GitHub searches, including separate comment searches. Inspected nearest issues do not cover the shared blank ingredient-ID defect. A new narrowly scoped source/consumer tracking issue is justified if primary recipe captures substantiate shared-ID reuse for distinct preparations; root owns final filing decision.",
  "proposed_issue_owner": "Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe for source ingestion/recipe-occurrence identity preservation, with MediaDive authoritative source correction as the underlying dependency. MIM can link the blocked source-only canary without minting a record.",
  "proposed_correction": "Retain every native recipe occurrence, original compound_id1944, blank label and full attribute; do not globally rewrite1944 to yeast, Trypticase or MES. Reconcile each preparation with original recipe/source and corrected authoritative native ingredient identifiers before any source-ID-to-MIM mapping. Verify downstream recipe occurrence identity remains source scoped.",
